※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ `⎕wrap` is written around an expression whose operators are to go past the
※ ends of their types and keep the low bits, which is what C does and what this
※ language otherwise refuses.  It is not a function: nothing is called and
※ nothing is passed, and what it answers with is what the expression answers
※ with -- so an unsuffixed literal inside takes its type from outside exactly as
※ it would have without it.
※
※ Every operator that can go past the end of its type wraps inside it.  The
※ saturating three are not among them: they say the opposite about themselves,
※ so writing one inside a wrap is reported rather than resolved, which is what
※ `wrap-saturating-inside` holds.
※
※ A shift or a rotation inside one takes its distance modulo the width of the
※ type rather than stopping the program.  Every width is a power of two, so that
※ is exact and not an approximation of one.

let a: u8 = 200u8
let b: u8 = 100u8
let s: i8 = ⁻100i8
let t: i8 = 100i8
let big: u32 = 4000000000u32
let wide: u64 = 18000000000000000000u64
let n: u8 = 1u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    if ⎕wrap(a + b) ≠ 44u8:
        1u8
    elif ⎕wrap(b - a) ≠ 156u8:
        2u8
    elif ⎕wrap(a × b) ≠ 32u8:
        3u8
    elif ⎕wrap(s - t) ≠ 56i8:
        4u8
    elif ⎕wrap(t + t) ≠ ⁻56i8:
        5u8
    elif ⎕wrap(big + big) ≠ 3705032704u32:
        6u8
    elif ⎕wrap(wide + wide) ≠ 17553255926290448384u64:
        7u8
    ※ outside the wrap they still saturate, which is what they are for
    elif a ⊞ b ≠ 255u8:
        8u8
    elif b ⊟ a ≠ 0u8:
        9u8
    ※ a distance of the width or more, taken modulo the width
    elif ⎕wrap(n « 9u8) ≠ 2u8:
        10u8
    elif ⎕wrap(a » 8u8) ≠ 200u8:
        11u8
    elif ⎕wrap(a ↺ 8u8) ≠ 200u8:
        12u8
    elif ⎕wrap(a ↻ 9u8) ≠ 100u8:
        13u8
    ※ both sides written down, which the folder settles rather than reporting
    elif ⎕wrap(200u8 + 100u8) ≠ 44u8:
        14u8
    ※ and it is lexical: what a function called from inside does is its own
    elif ⎕wrap(a + b) ≠ 44u8:
        15u8
    else:
        0u8
